ReplayKit patch 4 of 4 for win-capture-audio 2.3.4 (Ayrton09, commit d11b381).

The objects wasapi calls back into (the notification clients of the session monitor) were value members of the
watchers that registered them, although they are COM objects that the audio service holds by pointer and counts
references on. When a program ends, the service reports it on its own thread while the monitor thread unregisters and
destroys the watcher, so a callback or a release that is still on its way reaches the freed member and writes into the
heap. That is the kind of damage that ends in a heap corruption fast fail some minutes later (exception 0xc0000374, seen
on 2026-10-06 in the same obs session as the crash that patch 3 handles). The objects are now made with Make<>() and held
in ComPtr, so they live as long as wasapi still has a reference and are freed by the last release.

